From 0291ca00e7284abe1d48bc512035591d6aabc58d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:09:22 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 28/39] Stick: a full diagonal reaches the PSP nub's corner

A modern stick's gate is a circle, so at a full diagonal each axis is only
about 0.71 of its travel, and the left stick passed that on to the nub. The
PSP's nub reaches its corners, and a game that treats each axis on its own
sees a modern stick's diagonal as a smaller push, or none: a game with a
per-axis dead zone of 100 out of 127.5 read every full diagonal as no input
at all, and 22.5 degrees off a straight push as 0.64 of one.

input/stick.hpp maps the stick to the nub as a vector: the dead zone on its
length (as before), full deflection from 0.95 of the radius, then circle to
square, stretching the vector along its own direction until its longer axis
is its length, so a full push in any direction reaches the edge of the
square and a diagonal its corner. Each axis is rounded to the nearest step
and both ends are reached: -1 is 0 rather than 1. The keyboard's stick keys
and the on-screen stick go through the same rounding and square.

On by default. input.stick_square, the controls page's "Full diagonals"
row, turns the square off; <prefix>_NO_STICK_SQUARE does the same. Checks
in tests/input_tests.cpp. The right stick is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
